ermany  afterwards seeing as they let off seven  of the more important criminals how  would how would you trust the German  physicians after the war the German  physicians after there were I understood  that there were between two and three  hundred German doctors who were involved  in experiments but we only were able to  get twenty now in 1945 a very important  trial occurred in Dachau this was an  American military court trial in which  they they convicted dr. Schelling  some of the most infamous of the doctors  and hanged them there I mean we hanged a  you know seven Dachau hanged close to 40  now I do not know I cannot answer a  question about the doctors subsequently  but I think it's not a happy answer  there are too many doctors who were  involved in these experiments who got  away and who are still involved today  even in their 80s in the medical  practice I hope I am correct on that I  have my doctor expert up here yes  given the number of genocide Oh  massacres that have occurred in the last  50 years like Indonesia Cambodia Rwanda  what do you think we've learned the  answer to your question is we haven't  that's all I can say genocides are  continuing we haven't had I think that's  a question that I point out in my book  why haven't we learned the lessons  this is dr. Ming Lee tried in absentia  at your trial you know he asked a good  question  everybody wants to know about dr.  Mengele Josef Mengele who was the the  angel of death at Auschwitz who  experimented on children who would stand  at the ramp and select the the pregnant  Jews to save them so that when their  babies were born he could experiment on  them Mengele was hiding in a stable in  Germany all the time I worked there he  got away  he actually was in Auschwitz when the  Russian armies are got to Auschwitz and  he knew it would the EM was coming so he  ne his band of six or seven left and  started walking to Germany and when they  got to the border by that time American  military policemen